<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 4272 0 R/Alt(Plot of log luminosity, from 40.5 to 43.5, against days, from 0 to 160, for four Type Ia supernovae (SN1991T, SN1989B, SN1992A, SN1991bg) and the Type Ic SN1994I, each with a model curve. All rise steeply to a peak at about 15 to 20 days, at log L between about 42.2 and 43.4, and then decline smoothly; brighter supernovae decline more slowly.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 18784 0 R>>
